                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#9ea3b0",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "The panel replaces the centred dialog (owner, 2026-11-02, #1543). Power options rise as a 760 px panel anchored bottom-centre, 48 px above the edge, over whatever screen is up: here Settings, usually the stage. The body has three variants: a named session (\"Playback stops and <name> is saved first.\"), an unnamed one (\"Playback stops and this session is saved first. You name it before it saves.\") and an empty one (\"Playback stops. This session is empty, so there is nothing to save.\"). The staged-update line at 18 px appears only when an update is staged. The 7\" readout keeps the track display while the panel is up, and while Save As is open (owner, 2026-11-02, #1553). A screen shows only when it tells the player something: the player has just pressed the power key and is looking at the panel, so the old \"Power options on the main screen\" face told them nothing and hid the loops. The readout changes only once a save runs past 500 ms (Saving) or the goodbye comes."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
